config CPU_ACCEL
	tristate "Single CPU accelerator prototype"
	depends on SMP
	depends on MMU
	depends on GENERIC_IRQ_MIGRATION
	help
	  Build the first experimental single-CPU accelerator control plane and
	  architecture-staged lifecycle backend.

	  The prototype exposes /dev/cpu_accel. A control process selects one
	  online CPU, maps a shared control and sample area, and starts a bounded
	  timestamp workload. On x86 the target is entered through one staged IPI,
	  then runs with preemption and local interrupts disabled until completion
	  or recovery. This is a development experiment, not a production
	  isolation mechanism or a hard latency guarantee.
